<% content_for :title, 'Rulebook Search' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Rulebook Search' do %>
  <div class='space-y-8'>

    <p class='text-fg-muted'>
      Search across every rulebook this campaign has enabled and get back a ranked list of
      books, printed page numbers, and highlighted excerpts. The referee sees results from every
      enabled book; a player — anonymous, not-logged-in visitors, since this app has no separate
      player-account system — sees only the subset of enabled books also marked
      <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Player Searchable</span> on the
      <%= link_to 'Library', help_page_path('library'), class: 'no-underline hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2' %>
      page.
    </p>

    <div>
      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Search field</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Enter a word or short phrase, e.g. <span class='font-mono text-fg-bright'>jump drive</span>.
            Results update automatically as you type, after a short pause. Matches are found
            against the cleaned, searchable text extracted from each rulebook — not the exact
            wording of your query, so results include grammatical variants of your search terms.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Rulebook / Edition / Category filters</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Narrow results to a specific book, edition, or category. Only enabled — and, for
            players, player-searchable — rulebooks appear in these lists.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Results</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Results are grouped by rulebook, ordered by that book's strongest match, and
            collapsed by default — click a book's title to expand it. Within a book, each hit
            shows the page it was found on and a highlighted excerpt of the matching text.
            Weak, incidental matches on a common word are excluded automatically. A page showing
            <span class='font-mono text-fg-bright'>Unnumbered page</span> has no real printed
            page number — a cover, a blank page, or similar — and is identified by its position
            in the PDF instead.
          </dd>
          <div class='mt-3'>
            <p class='text-fg'>
              Only the first few hits per book are shown initially. If a book has more matches
              than that, an ellipsis appears at the bottom of its result group — click it to load
              the rest.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0804RS
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>
